<p>MRI information from Non-human models offers a unique perspective into general neural functioning and allows for a complement of experimental techniques not available in human specimens&#8230;</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>In a study measuring the association of temporal and frontal regions across several primate species, qualitative probabilistic tractography was performed on DTI image data to offer insight into the strength of this association. <img class="alignnone size-full wp-image-203" alt="Non-human MRI" src="https://web.archive.org/web/20200222234635im_/http://www.drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/pic4.png" width="442" height="371" srcset="https://web.archive.org/web/20200224105019im_/http://drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/pic4.png 779w, https://web.archive.org/web/20200224105019im_/http://drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/pic4-300x252.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 442px) 100vw, 442px"/></p>
<p>These images can then be quantified digitally to allow comparison of this association across various species.</p>
<p><a href="/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/01/nonhuman.png"><img class="size-full wp-image-399 alignnone" alt="nonhuman" src="https://web.archive.org/web/20200224105019im_/http://drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/01/nonhuman.png" width="689" height="223" srcset="https://web.archive.org/web/20200224105019im_/http://drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/01/nonhuman.png 689w, https://web.archive.org/web/20200224105019im_/http://drgutman.org/dglab_wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2013/01/nonhuman-300x97.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 689px) 100vw, 689px"/></a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>This would also be a good place to put some of the mouse brain imaging that Sam is involved with&#8230;</p>